invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: alpn_offered keeps the first name the client listed instead of the
  lowest index in the caller's offer, so the client's preference decides
  where RFC 7301 §3.2 has the server's decide. test/srv_parser_tests.h
  offers http/1.1 before h2 against a hello that lists h2 first and
  requires index 0.

--- old
            if (p->ch->alpn_selected == CH_ALPN_NONE || j < p->ch->alpn_selected) {
--- new
            if (p->ch->alpn_selected == CH_ALPN_NONE) {
